WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.660
Fate, guns, and a loveable Japanese mascot.&nbsp;
The final act of Bullet Train is jam-packed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:12.240
with tie-ins, callbacks, and double-crosses.&nbsp;
Here's how it all plays out. Spoilers ahead!

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:17.520
The third act of "Bullet Train" begins with&nbsp;
Kimura's father, the Elder, boarding the train&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:23.040
at the stop right before Kyoto. Except for a few&nbsp;
key characters, there's no one left on the train,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.760
something the White Death ensured&nbsp;
by buying out all the other seats.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.660
Somehow the Elder is aware of what's&nbsp;
been happening there, so when Prince,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.700
the first person he meets on the now largely&nbsp;
empty train, informs him his son has perished,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:42.000
he tells her she's mistaken. As Prince storms off,&nbsp;
the Elder joins Ladybug to discover that Kimura&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.220
is indeed alive. Surprisingly Lemon, who was also&nbsp;
believed to have been murdered by Prince, is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:53.100
ticking too. Nonetheless, the train contains an&nbsp;
excessive number of bodies, including the Hornet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.620
the Wolf, and Tangerine, not to mention the&nbsp;
White Death's mysteriously murdered son.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:04.200
As they approach Kyoto station, the quartet of men&nbsp;
forms an uneasy alliance in the hopes that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.700
don't become the White Death's next victims. Of&nbsp;
course, against the White Death's mass of goons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.620
there's not all that much of a stand they can&nbsp;
make, but they're determined to try. Lemon moves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.760
to the front of the train to see if he can take&nbsp;
control of it, the Elder waits to confront the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.200
White Death after years of planning his revenge&nbsp;
against the crime boss for murdering his wife,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.880
"Nooooooo! The White Death&nbsp;
had taken everything from me."

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.120
and, despite his terrible luck, Ladybug decides to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.837
put himself first in the line of fire&nbsp;
as they reach the end of the line.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.220
As the train comes to a stop,&nbsp;
Ladybug exits allowing both he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.180
and the viewers to see the White Death for&nbsp;
the first time on the station platform.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:47.160
Up until this point, the White Death is treated&nbsp;
much like Bill from Quentin Tarantino's two-part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.780
film, "Kill Bill." He is often mentioned&nbsp;
and his presence hangs like a shroud over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.280
the proceedings. And just like Bill, the&nbsp;
White Death’s face is only shown later on.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:01.200
Unfortunately for Ladybug, the White Death&nbsp;
thinks he is actually a man named Carver,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.180
Ladybug's hated co-worker who bowed out of&nbsp;
the job that Ladybug is currently trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:11.340
survive. Carver was responsible for staging the&nbsp;
accident that killed the White Death's wife. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.600
the White Death has gone out of his way to ensure&nbsp;
that every assassin who had something to do with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:21.180
the incident is on the train so he can take them&nbsp;
all out at once. He's happy to start with Ladybug,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.320
despite Ladybug's protests that he&nbsp;
isn't the man the White Death thinks.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:30.240
Before the White Death dispatches Ladybug,&nbsp;
the two henchmen who have been ordered to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:35.160
open the briefcase Ladybug was supposed to&nbsp;
steal finally complete their task. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.780
earlier in the film, Prince got Kimura to&nbsp;
crack the case's code and rigged it to blow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:45.000
when it was opened again. So as soon as the White&nbsp;
Death's goons lift the case's lid, it explodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.380
blowing Ladybug back onto the unmoving&nbsp;
train, followed by the White Death and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:53.640
several henchmen. This buys Ladybug enough&nbsp;
time to escape the White Death's clutches.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:58.020
The White Death is also distracted&nbsp;
by another issue, Prince, whose every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:02.160
move has been about assassinating the crime&nbsp;
lord. When the White Death enters the train,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.100
he's confronted by Prince, and she makes it clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.700
that the reason she's so determined to&nbsp;
take him out is that he's her father.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.120
Prince's grievance seems to be that&nbsp;
the White Death never paid attention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:16.500
to her because she's a girl. While most people&nbsp;
would seek therapy to cope with the rejection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:21.060
Prince has gone another way, and even&nbsp;
as she waves a gun in her father's face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:26.880
she still pursues her endgame. Her father is known&nbsp;
for killing anyone who crosses him, and Prince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.680
expects that's exactly what he'll do to her.&nbsp;
However, earlier in the movie, in anticipation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:36.900
of this exact moment, Prince rigs her gun to&nbsp;
backfire, killing whoever pulls the trigger.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:42.660
Despite her tears, Prince is actually anticipating&nbsp;
besting her father. Unfortunately, while the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:48.414
White Death accepts the gun, he declines to kill&nbsp;
Prince, leaving her feeling slighted once again.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:54.120
The White Death next encounters the Elder, who the&nbsp;
White Death recognizes as one of his predecessor's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:58.860
henchmen. Years ago, the Elder was suspicious&nbsp;
of the White Death and warned his boss of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:03.960
duplicitous nature. Unfortunately, his boss&nbsp;
didn't listen, resulting in the White Death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:09.540
taking over his entire operation and setting fire&nbsp;
to the Elder's house, killing the Elder's wife.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.200
The irony is that even though the two men&nbsp;
hold deep grudges against one another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.600
both are motivated by the demise of their spouses.&nbsp;
In other circumstances, they might have been part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.280
of a great support system for one another, but&nbsp;
neither character has any plans to hug it out now.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.120
The pair begins a brutal brawl just&nbsp;
as Lemon figures out how to get the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.960
train moving again. However, since Lemon&nbsp;
has made it clear that the kids' series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.340
"Thomas &amp; Friends," which revolves around the&nbsp;
anthropomorphized train Thomas the Tank Engine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:40.380
is his personal guide to life, the opportunity&nbsp;
to drive a train has to be a thrill for him.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.720
Whatever thrill Lemon feels quickly wears off&nbsp;
when he realizes he doesn't know how to control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:51.060
the train. It's traveling at breakneck speed and&nbsp;
he can't slow it down. If that weren't bad enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.560
as Ladybug joins him, he points out that they're&nbsp;
on a collision course with another train coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:00.300
in the opposite direction on the same track.&nbsp;
When a group of the White Death's goons appears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:05.220
Lemon volunteers to take them on, leaving Ladybug&nbsp;
to the bigger challenge of stopping the train.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:10.620
Each of them tries their best, but the trains&nbsp;
still collide in a spectacular crash. Yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:15.840
against all odds, the train Ladybug, Lemon,&nbsp;
and the others are on endures a substantial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.400
amount of damage but manage to stay on&nbsp;
the tracks. Despite that small victory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.560
the train is still hurtling down the tracks with&nbsp;
no signs of stopping, so Ladybug continues to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:29.820
work on figuring out the emergency brake&nbsp;
as Lemon fights the White Death's goons.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.940
Apparently, working with&nbsp;
Ladybug instead of against him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:36.872
as he has most of the train ride,&nbsp;
makes Lemon feel a bit warm and fuzzy.

00:05:37.208 --> 00:05:40.724
"Sorry I shot you twice!"

00:05:40.724 --> 00:05:43.823
"Thanks, man! That shows real growth." 

00:05:43.823 --> 00:05:48.000
While Ladybug is touched, the moment doesn't&nbsp;
last because as the train speeds over a bridge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.140
Lemon jumps out of the train with one of&nbsp;
the White Death's men into the water below.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:55.680
Elsewhere on the train, the battle&nbsp;
between the Elder and the White&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.760
Death continues. The men initially&nbsp;
seem well-matched. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:04.440
the White Death quickly manages to turn things&nbsp;
around. After all, you don't earn the nickname&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:09.000
the White Death if you aren't accustomed to&nbsp;
doling out a substantial amount of, well, death.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.680
For a moment, it looks like the White Death is&nbsp;
going to add the Elder to his undoubtedly lengthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:18.660
list of victims. But then Kimura, who, between&nbsp;
being shot in the gut and massively hung over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:23.460
hasn't been especially useful until this point,&nbsp;
picks up a water bottle rolling along the floor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:27.900
and tosses it at the White Death's head, stopping&nbsp;
him before he can deal his final death blow.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:32.580
As a flashback reveals, the water bottle has&nbsp;
played a key role throughout the story. Not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.940
only did Lemon get the bottle of water&nbsp;
for free while buying another beverage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:40.620
but it was also the water that Ladybug filled&nbsp;
with sleeping powder that Lemon drank just in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:45.660
time for it to kick in as Prince shot him, causing&nbsp;
her to believe she'd killed him. Once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:51.180
the water bottle shows up just in the nick of&nbsp;
time, ensuring Kimura can save his father's life.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:56.460
In the front of the train, Ladybug has finally&nbsp;
found the handbook with instructions in English,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:00.060
which includes information about&nbsp;
how to deploy the emergency brake.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:05.517
"We’re good! I got it! No!"

00:07:05.517 --> 00:07:10.500
So, Ladybug instead just pulls out the entire&nbsp;
emergency brake mechanism, wires and all.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:15.240
It gets the job done, but it isn't pretty.&nbsp;
The screeching brakes bring the train to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:20.580
a stop way too fast, causing it to jump the&nbsp;
tracks. As the train careens out of control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:24.120
the momentum causes Ladybug&nbsp;
to fall back through the cars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:28.920
and while he's hit in the head with a coffee pot&nbsp;
along the way, the bulbous costume of Momomon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:34.500
an anime character with its own themed car on the&nbsp;
train, breaks his fall. The vehicle finally comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:38.577
to an inelegant stop in the middle of what&nbsp;
appears to be an otherwise tranquil village.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.980
Ladybug, Kimura, and the Elder exit the&nbsp;
train. They're all worse for wear but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.700
miraculously still alive. They're&nbsp;
followed by a furious White Death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:52.200
He once again goes after Ladybug, whom&nbsp;
he still believes is Carver. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.800
his gun has run out of bullets, so&nbsp;
he grabs the gun he took from Prince,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:00.660
still unaware it has been rigged to backfire.&nbsp;
So, as soon as the White Death pulls the trigger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:06.120
the gun explodes in his face and he sinks to&nbsp;
the ground, dead and with half his head missing.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:10.200
Immediately afterward, an extremely&nbsp;
disheveled Prince appears in the doorway&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:14.637
of one of the remaining train cars. It's&nbsp;
unclear where she's been all this time.

00:08:14.637 --> 00:08:20.700
"It’s my luck that delivered my&nbsp;
father’s corpse at my feet." 
 &nbsp;

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.560
"The narcissism on this chick."

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.240
Fortunately, neither they nor the viewers have&nbsp;
to find out because a truck runs Prince over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:32.676
seemingly bringing her life to an end, or at&nbsp;
least setting her up for a lengthy hospital stay.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:37.980
As Ladybug, Kimura, and the Elder walk away&nbsp;
from the destruction of the train following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:42.840
Prince's demise, Ladybug's handler pulls&nbsp;
up in a car. While she tries to deny it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:47.460
Ladybug knows Maria's intention was to&nbsp;
rescue him. He's so touched that he gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:52.440
teary-eyed. As they walk back towards Maria's&nbsp;
car to leave, Ladybug informs her that he no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:57.000
longer believes in luck, especially his&nbsp;
bad luck. Now he just believes in fate.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:01.680
Ladybug's change of heart makes sense and&nbsp;
viewers may even feel it's a long time coming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.700
especially since throughout the movie&nbsp;
many of the things he's deemed bad luck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:10.140
could actually be seen as good if looked&nbsp;
at from another perspective. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:14.640
consider when he wasn't able to exit the train&nbsp;
earlier in the film as planned because the Wolf&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:18.660
was coming in the same door he was trying to&nbsp;
go out. While the Wolf's violent attack on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:23.520
him was unexpected, Ladybug ultimately&nbsp;
wasn't hurt badly and even managed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:27.960
inadvertently take out the Wolf before things&nbsp;
could spiral too out of control. Ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:33.240
it was a pretty positive result for Ladybug,&nbsp;
even if the situation wasn't exactly ideal.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.300
As Ladybug explains his new fate-based philosophy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:41.340
a pole falls over, crushing Maria's car. While&nbsp;
Ladybug might have previously chalked up the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:45.375
incident to his bad luck, now he wonders&nbsp;
if it could actually be a good thing.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:49.680
Viewers may not spend too much time thinking&nbsp;
about who was driving the truck that hit Prince.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:54.840
However, the movie uses a mid-credits scene to&nbsp;
fill in that blank before the film wraps up. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:58.740
movie flashes back to the moment after Lemon&nbsp;
jumps from the train and lands in the water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:03.120
below. He takes out the White Death's henchman&nbsp;
that fell with him, goes out of the water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:08.160
and finds a road where he sees a small truck&nbsp;
with a photo of lemons and tangerines on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:12.480
side. Lemon doesn't miss the not-so-subtle&nbsp;
symbolism and takes the truck as his own.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:15.600
Now that his brother and long-time&nbsp;
partner Tangerine is dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:19.080
it's not clear what could be next&nbsp;
for Lemon, but at least his getaway&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:23.280
seems to be going well. In perhaps what's&nbsp;
supposed to be a final commentary on fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:27.360
he drives into the village where the train&nbsp;
has crashed, and as he heads down the road,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:31.860
he sees Prince in front of him. Instead of&nbsp;
hitting the brakes, he presses the accelerator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:36.600
speeding into the young woman who tried to&nbsp;
kill him. With that final violent act, another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.740
in a long string of violent acts throughout&nbsp;
the movie, "Bullet Train" comes to an end.

